  "post": {
    "caption": "The Hortensia is a pale pink diamond of about 21 carats, flat and five sided. It was in the French crown jewels under Louis the Fourteenth, and its name honors Queen Hortense, though nothing shows she wore it. It went into a hair ornament for Empress Eugenie in 1856. When France sold most of its crown jewels in 1887, it was kept, and it still belongs to the Louvre.",
